<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Prompting Consistency Experiment</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Additional Results</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our self-consistency preliminary experiment, we additional examine the probability of different LLM-reported impressions to better understand their behavior. <a href="#A1.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ A.1 Additional Results ‣ Appendix A Prompting Consistency Experiment ‣ Artificial Impressions: Evaluating Large Language Model Behavior Through the Lens of Trait Impressions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 8</span></a> shows the gap in token probabilities between high and low impressions reported by the LLM (larger values representing higher probability of generating positive impressions). In nearly all cases (excluding Llama-3.2 (1B) in the 3rd-person setting), models are more likely and more confident in generating positive impressions than negative. Furthermore, <a href="#A1.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ A.1 Additional Results ‣ Appendix A Prompting Consistency Experiment ‣ Artificial Impressions: Evaluating Large Language Model Behavior Through the Lens of Trait Impressions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 9</span></a> reports the percentage of positive trait predictions among all messages, similarly showing that models are largely biased toward predicting positive traits. Such differences are particularly pronounced in the 1st-person setting among models, leading to the poor consistency we observe in <a href="#S3" title="3 Preliminary Study: Prompt-based Impressions ‣ Artificial Impressions: Evaluating Large Language Model Behavior Through the Lens of Trait Impressions" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section 3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
